```sql
-- Description / Thinking process:
-- Objective: Identify how the seven target countries (United States, France, China, Italy, Spain, Germany, Iran)
-- appear in the CONFIRMED_CASES table.  Earlier use of ANY(ARRAY[…]) failed because Snowflake does not
-- support that syntax.  The alternative is to use REGEXP_LIKE with a single pattern that OR-joins the
-- country names (“|”).  Adding the 'i' flag makes the search case-insensitive.  DISTINCT eliminates
-- duplicates, and LIMIT 20 keeps the output concise.
SELECT DISTINCT "country_or_region"
FROM COVID19_JHU_WORLD_BANK.COVID19_JHU_CSSE.CONFIRMED_CASES
